    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d94">

                <pb facs="0190" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">295.1122/6–2650: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-06-26T23:00:00+10:00">June 26, 1950, 11
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 26—9:31 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>957. In view of rapid deterioration and disintegration, I am immediately starting
                    evacuation of all females toward south. All indications are that situation is
                    disintegrating so rapidly that we may not all be able to get out particularly in
                    view of fighting at Ascom and Kimpo. Plan is to follow road toward Taejon by
                    motor vehicle.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d94-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Repeated information CINCFE unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d94-f1" n="1" xml:id="d94-f1-content">
                <p>Notes on the source text indicate that an advance copy of this telegram was sent
                    to the Bureau of Far Eastern Affairs at 10:05 a. m. and also that it was relayed
                    to the Defense Department at 10:30 a. m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
